  actor: jgstern_agent  # a9ee
  clock: 5  # a9ee
  nonce: a9ee  # a9ee
  message: "DONE for the PYTHON half in PR #2025 (merged; dev bb7e70cf48); the SCALA half (zio-http Routes(...) emits no usage context) is a different producer, filed as WI-pohis-zunar-poluh-kosiz-dutad-juris-rasik-rimad. py.py stamps meta[\"parent_base_classes\"] on every method of a class with bases (the class symbol's base_classes list, the java/objc pass-1.5 shape); a method of a baseless class and a free function carry no key. graphql-python.yaml regains the Graphene resolver rule in the supported spelling (method_name ^resolve_\\w+$ + parent_base_class ^(graphene\\.)?ObjectType$ -> graphql_resolver), replacing the WI-hapon note. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: the item's own fixture shape, `class Query(graphene.ObjectType): def resolve_hello` -> Query.resolve_hello carries graphql_resolver; `class Todo(Resource): def get` -> Todo.get carries route_handler (both through enrich_symbols with the framework detected); Todo.helper, Plain.get and a free `get` carry neither. Production-path test packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_py_parent_base_classes.py; mutation (drop the stamp) reddens the three rule/stamp cases, the absence control stays green. CORPUS (lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sorop_11032026/: PREREGISTER.md, RESULT.md, diff_*.txt; per-symbol concept diff + entrypoint sets, base = dev e0dec7418e): flask-restful (flask-restful-test is the same clone) gains route_handler on 49 methods, all verb-named methods of a Resource subclass, 87/87 classes have bases, 437/437 methods stamped, 0 methods of a baseless class carry the key; mlflow gains graphql_resolver on exactly the 7 pre-registered resolve_* methods of its direct ObjectType subclasses (autogenerated_graphql_schema.py) and on none of the 8 resolve_* methods elsewhere; no concept lost on either. ENTRYPOINTS: route_handler maps to no EntrypointKind (falcon, flask-restful, nex emit it; entrypoints.py never reads it), so flask-restful's are unchanged and WI-fuzik's withhold still cannot see a flask-restful handler -- WI-losij adds the mapping with its flip test. graphql_resolver maps to graphql_server: mlflow +7 graphql_server, -7 library_export at the 500 cap (the displacement WI-vumig is about). Pre-registration 4 (\"no entrypoint change\") was REFUTED by that known mapping, which I had not accounted for; not a new consumer. NOT REACHED (filed WI-pazok-dunit-zibik-ravad-suhuf-puvit-tatar-donas): a resolver on a subclass of an in-repo ObjectType subclass (mlflow Query(QueryType), Mutation(MutationType), 4 real resolvers), because base_class / parent_base_class rules match declared bases only, every language. NOT ASSERTED: that every python method-level rule now fires; only parent_base_class + method_name was unblocked."  # a9ee
